course: dictionary
lesson: 14541
title: Formal words: pertain
level: primary-6
stars: 3
explain: Pertain is a formal word. You will meet it in rules, official letters and school notices. It usually means to be about something, or to be connected with it. «The questions pertaining to fractions are on page five.» The questions are about fractions, so pertaining to means about or connected with.
explain: Pertain is almost always followed by "to". Try your meaning in the sentence: «The rules pertaining to safety must be followed.» Ask yourself: what could I say instead? "The rules about safety" still makes sense, so pertaining to means about.
explain: Pertain can also mean to apply in a certain situation. «This rule does not pertain to children under ten.» The rule does not apply to them. When you see pertain in a formal text, read the words after "to" to find out what it is about.
fact: Pertain is a verb, so its forms are pertain, pertains, pertained and pertaining.
fact: «Pertain to» means to be about, be connected with, or belong to something.
fact: «Pertaining to» means about, as in «questions pertaining to fractions», which means questions about fractions.
fact: Pertain can also mean to apply in a certain situation, as in «The rule pertains only to adults.»
fact: Pertain is a formal word. In everyday talk, you could use "about", "for" or "applies to" instead.
exercise: «The questions pertaining to fractions are on page five.» What does pertaining to mean here? | Missing from | *About or connected with | Written in pencil | Far away from
exercise: «The rules pertaining to safety must be followed.» Which everyday word could replace pertaining to without changing the meaning? | Lost in | *About | Against | Instead of
exercise: What does pertain mean in «This rule does not pertain to children under ten»? | Is written for | Is written in a book | *Applies to | Is broken by
test: What does «pertain to» mean? | Go under | Fall off | *Be about or belong to | Run away from
test: «The old law pertains to all drivers.» What does pertains to mean here? | Is written in gold | Is lost in the post | *Applies to | Has nothing to do with
exam: In «The guidance pertaining to homework is in the letter», what does pertaining to mean? | Ruining | Asking for | Hidden under | *Connected with
